Filter the rows, then chain a locator inside the match:

```ts
const row = page.getByRole('row').filter({ hasText: 'Oncology' });
await row.getByRole('button', { name: 'Edit' }).click();
```

explain:
`innerText()` returns the rendered text of the element.

```ts
const text = await page.locator('.message').innerText();
console.log(text);
```

Alternative:

```ts
const text = await page.locator('.message').textContent();
```

`locator.count()` returns the number of matching elements, so a count above 0 means the element exists.

```ts
const count = await page.locator('.user').count();
expect(count).toBeGreaterThan(0);
```

Or use an assertion:

```ts
await expect(page.locator('#item')).toHaveCount(1);
```

q:
What happens here?

```ts
await page.locator('#login').click();
await page.close();
```

What happens here?

```ts
const locator = page.locator('.item');
await page.reload();
await locator.click();
```

What will fail?

```ts
const el = await page.$('#btn');
await page.reload();
await el.click();
```

What is the output?

```ts
if (await page.locator('#btn').isVisible()) {
  console.log('Visible');
}
```

What will happen if only 3 matching elements exist?

```ts
const locator = page.locator('.item');
await locator.nth(5).click();
```

explain:
Wait for the real condition, the spinner going away, instead of guessing. `force: true` skips the actionability checks and can hide real bugs, a fixed `waitForTimeout` is slow and flaky, and blind retries just repeat the problem.

```ts
await expect(page.locator('.spinner')).toBeHidden();
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit' }).click();
```
